course: dictionary
lesson: 8102
title: Rend: tear, break, hurt
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Rend is an old word. You will mostly find it in old stories, poems, the Bible and fantasy books, not in everyday talk. It has three main meanings, and the context tells you which one fits.
explain: To rend means to tear something violently into pieces. «Rend your heart and not your garments» is from the Bible (Joel 2:13). In Bible times, sad people rent (tore) their clothes to show sorrow. Rent is the past tense of rend.
explain: Rend can also mean to break a silence or the air with a loud sound, or to cause great pain to someone's heart. «Heart-rending» means very sad. To check your meaning, swap in tear, break or hurt and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Rend means to tear something violently into pieces.
fact: Rend is the verb; rent is its past tense, as in «They rent their clothes».
fact: «Heart-rending» means very sad, so it is often used in sad stories.
fact: Rend can also mean to break a silence with a loud sound, as in «rend the air».
fact: Careful: rent (the money you pay for a home) sounds the same but is a different word.
exercise: «The storm began to rend the old sail in two.» What does rend mean here? | *To tear violently into pieces | To mend gently with a needle | To paint slowly | To tie tightly with rope
exercise: «Her story was heart-rending, and the whole room cried.» What does heart-rending mean? | *Very sad | Very cold | Very quiet | Very funny
exercise: «A sudden scream rent the silence of the night.» What does rent mean here? | *Broke the silence with a loud sound | Whispered softly | Covered in darkness | Slept deeply
test: In the Bible, people rent their clothes to show sorrow. What does rent mean here? | *Tore | Washed | Hid | Sold
test: Which word means very sad and painful to the heart? | Heart-warming | Heart-beat | Heart-shaped | *Heart-rending
exam: «The shout rent the air, and the birds flew away.» Which meaning of rend fits best? | *Broke the air with a loud sound | Gently stroked the air | Painted the sky a bright colour | Slept through the night
